===============================================================================
Third-party components
===============================================================================

1. Basic Pitch (note transcription model and decoder)
   https://github.com/spotify/basic-pitch
   Copyright Spotify AB — Apache License 2.0 (repository LICENSE)

   The onset / frame / minimum-length / contour note decoder in
   Packages/HearSheet (BasicPitchDecoder.swift) is a Swift port of Spotify's
   `basic_pitch/note_creation.py:model_output_to_notes`, keeping Spotify's
   default thresholds. The model graph is unchanged: waveform input
   [1, 43844, 1], note [1, 172, 88], onset [1, 172, 88],
   contour [1, 172, 264] heads.

   The Core ML weights shipped with the app are the published ICASSP 2022
   release checkpoint, used unmodified (pinned by SHA-256 in models.lock,
   fetched by scripts/fetch-models, never committed to git). The app loads
   whichever checkpoint models.lock pins; no app code depends on which
   checkpoint that is.

   Apache License 2.0: https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

2. LAME MP3 encoder 3.100 (Packages/LAME, vendored libmp3lame sources)
   https://lame.sourceforge.io
   Copyright 1999-2017 The LAME Project — GNU Library General Public
   License 2.0 (LGPL-2.0-or-later; see the upstream COPYING). Used only for
   the "Download MP3" export (Swift wrapper: Sources/App/MP3Encoder.swift).
   Only the encoder library sources are vendored; the decoder (mpglib),
   CLI frontend and x86 SIMD paths are excluded. Build notes and the file
   list are in Packages/LAME/VENDOR.md.

